  "dedup_reason": "Coordinator independently read15 ranges1167lines including full migration214/world storage204/contents source28/backpack handler38/Core item migration37/CodecHelper63 plus bounded actual wrapper and inventory load/extract/serialize/dirty. Conservative same-family merge with30cdabca3ee13fdaf65f: existing earned cargo is moved from inline item inventory to shared UUID world storage then consumed by real handlers, with source removed before durable ack. Sophisticated uses direct compound transfer and only absent UUID; Roots inserts typed herb slots and logs leftovers. Those are alternate policies within the already credited ownership transfer family. Current typed-field precedence and realCount-to-modern oversized codec conversion are useful format/amount boundaries but not independently evidenced new gameplay owner; no per-component/slot/DFU increment. Separate fixed Core and backpack snapshots have unproven matching release dependency, so no executable paired binary compatibility claim.25ab permission Clone is different but does not remove overlap with30cd.",
  "limits": [
    "No safe transaction: item UUID bound before target write, first inventory migrated/oldkey removed before second; exception can leave mixed state, existing UUID prevents retrying remaining inline keys. Source metadata and inventory live in distinct item/world files with no durable acknowledgement/atomicity.",
    "Existing current or migrated legacy UUID skips migrateBackpackContents completely even if custom_data still has inline cargo; subsequent handler resolves existing or creates empty target. No merge/collision/ownership ACL audit. Duplicate UUID stacks refer same world contents by design; not safe clone-by-root copying.",
    "normalizeLegacyData deletes all normalized metadata even when new key already exists. contains only/no typed tests on many legacy getters maps wrongtype to0/empty and may throw on UUID/ResourceLocation; no backup/opaque retention. Current field precedence explicit but no old/new equivalence proof.",
    "getOrCreateContentsUuid clears only noop handlers, setBackpackStack caches capacities/render but does not invalidate all previously real cached handlers. Reused wrapper replacement can still point old contents; full repository mutation/linkedstorage implementation not audited.",
    "BackpackStorage.get noarg routes by exact threadgroup/server availability, otherwise returns client copy. Thus normalization may mutate client ItemStack/clientcopy too; no claim migration server-authoritative in every call. linked endpoint uses separate canonical resolver not fully read and not counted.",
    "Core dependency is separately fixed snapshot a25986, backpack630357. Actual imports/call APIs read, but matching release dependency/version pin/build files not cached/proven; not a tested compatible binary. Native DataFixer modern internals and component codecs not audited; fixed3465 assumption not discovered historical source-version.",
    "Legacy Count processing only if no components key; existing components even wrongtype suppress DFU. realCount overrides normalized count if DFU returned different reference or current count missing; otherwise modern count wins over conflictingrealCount. count raw signedint, no clamp. Legacy id unknown may later codec fail; no missing-ID escrow.",
    "InventoryHandler ignores saved Size by setSize override retaining constructor capacity; out-of-range slots skipped, duplicate slots later valid overwrite, parse errors logged/empty/partial. deserializeNBT does not clear existing live slots first; reusedload missing/failed entry can retain old. initStackNbts creates fresh current list from valid slots; next save can omit invalid raw/unknown fields/outside slots.",
    "World load filters absent-accesslog emptyinventory/upgrades with nootherkeys, before any manual cleaning method; rawrecord may be dropped. We did not call removeNonPlayerBackpackContents or any filesystem deletion. load normalizes data but no explicit setDirty so rewrittenformat waitsotherchange.",
    "Actual upgraded inventory normalization shows migration pipeline; full UpgradeHandler consumer implementation and all insertion/partitioner/slottracker hooks not reread, no claim all upgrade behaviors/runtimelosslessness. Native SavedData persistence and actual player save/clone/death not tested.",
    "No network/game/production/checklist/ledger edits/commit/push. Fixed modern APIs not Forge1.20.1 adoption proof."
